WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.127
Use this guide when deciding how to reshape.

00:00:02.127 --> 00:00:06.837
If category values should become columns, pivot with conditional aggregation.

00:00:06.837 --> 00:00:10.702
If columns should become rows, use UNION ALL or lateral VALUES.

00:00:10.702 --> 00:00:13.457
Keep dynamic categories long when possible.

00:00:13.457 --> 00:00:16.192
Use a wide form for stable matrix reporting.

00:00:16.192 --> 00:00:21.117
And whenever several source rows map to one cell, make the aggregate decision explicit.

00:00:21.117 --> 00:00:26.447
Connect this idea to a BI dashboard turning monthly categories into presentation columns.

00:00:26.447 --> 00:00:31.117
Ask what could go wrong if the concept were misunderstood: could rows be duplicated,

00:00:31.117 --> 00:00:37.747
important records disappear, categories be interpreted incorrectly, or a report become difficult to reproduce?

00:00:37.747 --> 00:00:42.452
A strong analyst can explain both the SQL operation and the assumption behind it.

00:00:42.452 --> 00:00:47.440
After the example, summarize the idea in one plain-language sentence before moving on.
